ames></name><name><surname>Rose</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Massie</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Chatterjee</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Waters</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The utility of gestures in patients with chest discomfort</article-title><source>Am J Med</source><year>2007</year><volume>120</volume><fpage>83</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17208083</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.amjmed.2006.05.045</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Peabody</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Luck</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Glassman</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Dresselhaus</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of vignettes, standardized patients, and chart abstraction: a prospective validation study of 3 methods for measuring quality</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2000</year><volume>283</volume><fpage>1715</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10755498</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.283.13.1715</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Feldman</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><name><surname>Freund</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Burns</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Moskowitz</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kasten</surname><given-names>LE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nonmedical influences on medical decision making: an experimental technique using videotapes, factorial design, and survey sampling</article-title><source>Health Serv Res</source><year>1997</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>343</fpage><lpage>66</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9240285</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McKinlay</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Freund</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Moskowitz</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The unexpected influence of physician attributes on clinical decisions: Results of an experiment</article-title><source>J Health Soc Behav</source><year>2002</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>92</fpage><lpage>106</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11949199</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/3090247</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gillies</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name><name><surname>Chenok</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Shortell</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Pawlson</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Wimbush</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The impact of health plan delivery system organization on clinical quality and patient satisfaction</article-title><source>Health Serv Res</source><year>2006</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>1181</fpage><lpage>99</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16899002</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>